<title>UK: UK's Major hails falling jobless rate.</title>
<headline>UK's Major hails falling jobless rate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major said on Wednesday that the latest jobless figures showed  Britain was booming.</p>
<p>&quot;Today's news is proof that Britain is booming. Unemployment is down to its lowest level for well over six years,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Falling unemployment, stable prices, lower taxes, higher living standards - people's hard work has created a turbo-economy, which is making life better right across the country.</p>
<p>&quot;Only if we stick on this course can we be sure to make life better still.&quot;</p>
</text>
